{% markdown %}

Every post needs a hero image, and I kept putting it off. Stock photos feel wrong for a personal blog. I can't draw. Hunting for the right Creative Commons image was eating more time than writing the post itself.

AI image generation is cheap now -- a penny per image via [Together AI](https://www.together.ai/) running [FLUX.2-dev](https://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/FLUX.2-dev). But the default output looks like AI slop.

## The style is the whole trick

What made this work was constraining to a Japanese blockprint aesthetic: high-contrast black ink woodcut on cream paper, sparse warm amber accent, no gradients. Every prompt gets the same style prefix baked in.

A limited palette reads as a deliberate design choice, not a generated artifact. High contrast holds up at small sizes and in dark mode. More importantly, the consistency across posts looks like an intentional visual identity -- not a random collection of AI images.

